WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.590
A family business in your town
wants a new delivery truck.

2
00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.970
A tech startup wants new servers.

3
00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.020
Neither has the cash on hand.

4
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.040
Both go looking for a loan.

5
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.580
The loan comes with a
price tag of its own:

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:13.910
the interest rate.

7
00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.810
So where does the money
businesses borrow come from,

8
00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.800
and what decides its price?

9
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.960
In this mission, you'll draw
the loanable funds market,

10
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.290
and see why it is priced in real rates,

11
00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.730
not nominal ones.

12
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.510
Then you'll run a graph lab
on government borrowing,

13
00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:31.030
and trace money flowing in from abroad.

14
00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:33.390
Your mission: find out who lends,

15
00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.870
who borrows, and what sets the price.
